This research paper presents a novel unsupervised algorithm based on the EM algorithm for financial time-series clustering. It identifies and groups market regimes characterized by similar financial conditions, where a condition is defined as the output of a specified regression model. Evaluations were conducted using historical data from the S&P 500 index, a regression model incorporating several popular financial indicators, and two approaches for determining cluster numbers. Notably, the proposed method demonstrated superior performance in predicting market regime transitions compared to existing benchmark methods. Further analysis revealed that the S&P 500 index was more accurately forecasted when the algorithm was allowed to select a larger number of clusters, and that financial indicators related to volume, such as the bid-ask quotes ratio, played a significant predictive role. Ultimately, the proposed algorithm's effectiveness in predicting market regime transitions and its robustness in handling different indicator combinations were effectively validated. This research is expected to contribute to the development of more accurate models for predicting financial regime transitions. The relevant code is available for public access at https://github.com/jeanfranmontanari/REG-MC. This research was supported by the Brazilian National Council of Technological and Scientific Development (CNPq) under the grant number 477/2019. Regime Switching with the EM Algorithm for Financial Time-Series Clustering. This research was supported by the Brazilian National Council of Technological and Scientific Development (CNPq) under the grant number 477/2019. We would like to thank the reviewers for their insightful comments, which significantly improved the quality of this research. \bigskip \textbf{Supplementary Materials} 
